                <pb facs="0866" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg780"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-09-10"><hi rendition="#italic">September 10,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman states that Consul Ravndal reports that Beirut is quiet, but that
                    many of the shops are still closed, as the people have not entirely recovered
                    from their fright of last Sunday.)</p>
            </div>
